#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:6
msgid "Exercise: Turtle Graphics"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:8
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will create an incremental TT muncher macro called "
"`turtle_directions!`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:11
msgid ""
"Your macro will parse a domain-specific language (DSL) for turtle graphics "
"instructions which maintains its old-school style by omitting any "
"punctuation between instructions. This DSL will be used to construct a "
"`cons`\\-list-style `TurtleProgram` value."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:16
msgid "Turtle Operation DSL"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:18
msgid ""
"The `turtle_directions!` macro should parse the following unpunctuated "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:20
msgid "`FWD n`: moves forward by `n` steps (`TurtleProgram::Forward(n, rest)`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:21
msgid ""
"`REV n`: moves backward by `n` steps (`TurtleProgram::Reverse(n, rest)`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:22
msgid "`LEFT n`: turns left by `n` degrees (`TurtleProgram::Left(n, rest)`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:23
msgid "`RIGHT n`: turns right by `n` degrees (`TurtleProgram::Right(n, rest)`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:24
msgid "`PEN UP`: lifts the pen (`TurtleProgram::PenUp(rest)`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:25
msgid "`PEN DOWN`: lowers the pen (`TurtleProgram::PenDown(rest)`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:26
msgid ""
"`RED` and `BLACK`: set the pen color (`TurtleProgram::SetColor(color, rest)`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:28
msgid ""
"Where `rest` is a `Box<TurtleProgram>` representing the remaining steps of "
"the program."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:31
msgid "Implement the `turtle_directions!` macro in the following program:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:51
msgid "// TODO: Implement the `turtle_directions!` macro.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/token-munchers/exercise.md:93
msgid ""
"Highlight how matching on specific keyword token sequences (e.g. `PEN UP`, "
"`RED`, or `FWD n`) at the head of the token stream allows parsing each "
"command according to the number and kind of expected tokens to follow."
msgstr ""
